# A7 6.05  Distance on the Coordinate Plane — MA.8.GR.1.2 (MN 6.5). Two points on one horizontal line: subtract the
# x's (across zero the two pieces add — the state's named misconception is (−2, 0) to (3, 0) as 1). On one vertical
# line: the y's. A slanted segment is the hypotenuse of a right triangle drawn on the grid: its legs are read from
# the coordinates, then a² + b² = c². No distance formula (Clarification 2); every radicand a whole number up to 225
# with no square factor. From board 4 on the grid shows the two points and nothing else, as the book's test does.
# Built from the benchmark and the B1G-M first (the unit outline), then read against Math Nation 6.5 (A7 Unit 6 Audit).
